foundation.question_text:
The hyperbola $y = \dfrac{1}{x}$ has vertical asymptote $x = 0$ and horizontal asymptote $y = 0$.
State the equations of the asymptotes of $y = \dfrac{1}{x + 3} - 4$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.75]
\draw[->] (-4.5,0) -- (4.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-4.5) -- (0,4.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-4,-2,2,4} {\draw (\x,0.15) -- (\x,-0.15); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.15) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {-4,-2,2,4} {\draw (0.15,\y) -- (-0.15,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.1,-0.1) {$O$};
\draw[dashed,thick,red] (0,-4.2) -- (0,4.2);
\node[above left,red] at (0,3.8) {$x=0$};
\draw[dashed,thick,red] (-4.2,0) -- (4.2,0);
\node[above,red] at (3.0,0.15) {$y=0$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=0.25:4.0,smooth,samples=50,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{1/\x});
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-4.0:-0.25,smooth,samples=50,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{1/\x});
\node[blue,above right] at (1.2,1.2) {$y=\dfrac{1}{x}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
The graph of $y = |x|$ is transformed into $y = -2|x - 3| + 8$.
Find the coordinates of its vertex and its $x$-intercepts.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (-4.5,0) -- (4.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.5) -- (0,4.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,0.1) -- (\x,-0.1); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {1,2,3,4} {\draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick, <->] (-3.5,3.5) -- (0,0) -- (3.5,3.5);
\fill (0,0) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above left] at (2.5,2.5) {$y=|x|$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
